tonight a man accused of driving drunk  and killing a mother of three near  durango and russell on thanksgiving back  in 2019  is sentenced after taking a plea deal  nathan postel will spend  eight years in prison with a max of 20  years  8 news now reporter madison kimbrough  sat down with the mother and brother of  the victim  who say they finally feel some sense of  closure  yes monique's family watched as they  watched the man  accused of killing the mother of three  finally sentenced this was on monday  i spoke with the family about how  they're doing a year and a half later  after the crash  and what this all means to them so we  went into this small room  and we waited and this woman came in and  she was wearing a uniform  and on her uniform she had the letters  coroner's office in gold  and before she could say anything i  looked at her and i said my daughter's  dead  isn't she monique prado a daughter  sister and mother  of three her life taken in an instant as  she and her eldest daughter went out for  a coffee run thanksgiving morning  in 2019. her family speaking out after  monday's sentencing  said after postel reached a plea deal  for killing prado  while driving under the influence of  alcohol and cocaine  i thought the judge was fair  i she listened to everything we had to  say on both sides  and and i feel the sentence that he got  which was the maximum of 20 years  was deserved these were his actions  nobody else caused this  prado's family didn't have high  expectations giving prior sentences  they've seen with similar cases  so when they heard the verdict they  immediately felt a sense of closure we  can begin the grieving process  we can begin to heal and we can begin to  move forward with our lives because  we've been stuck for the past year and a  half postdale will be eligible for  parole  after eight years but could spend up to  20 years in prison  this has impacted our lives and the  lives of her children  we are responsible for our choices that  we make  he made some really bad choices that  resulted in  the death of someone  and mr postel did have a prior felony  that was in 2014 before this crash  even happened that was for possession of  a controlled  substance reporting live madison  kimbrough 8 news now
 

